flow "Bulkhead isolation"
summary "Partitions concurrency into separate pools per dependency so one slow downstream service cannot starve unrelated traffic."
tags resilience fault-tolerance concurrency
level intermediate
source "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/patterns/bulkhead"
related distributed-systems/circuit-breaker distributed-systems/retry-backoff-dlq

node client "Clients" actor
node api "API Gateway" service tone=primary
group pools "Isolated thread pools"
node p-pay "Payments Pool (1/4)" state in=pools
node p-cat "Catalog Pool (1/4)" state in=pools
node pay "Payments API" service
node cat "Catalog API" service
edge client > api
edge api > p-pay
edge api > p-cat
edge p-pay > pay
edge p-cat > cat

scenario isolated "Separate pools keep dependencies independent"
  step normal "Traffic flows through dedicated pools"
    "Like watertight compartments in a ship's hull, the gateway assigns separate bounded thread pools (4 slots each) to Payments and Catalog."
    send client > api "checkout + browse"
    send api > p-pay "charge"
    send api > p-cat "list items" with
    send p-pay > pay "charge"
    send p-cat > cat "list" with
    state p-pay,p-cat,pay,cat success

scenario saturate "Slow Payments saturates its pool only" from=isolated/normal
  step pay-hangs "Payments API slows to a crawl"
    "Payments begins stalling for 30s per call. In-flight checkout requests quickly occupy all 4 slots in the Payments Pool."
    detail "When a consumer calls a slow or unresponsive service, each in-flight call holds onto pool resources (threads or connections) until it finishes or times out. In a shared pool, continued requests to the failing dependency eventually exhaust the pool and block calls to every healthy dependency too."
    state pay error
    effect pay shake
    send api > p-pay "4 slow calls"
    label p-pay "Payments Pool (4/4 FULL)"
    state p-pay error with
    callout p-pay "Pool exhausted: 4/4 busy"
  step reject-pay "Extra Payments calls fast-fail"
    "A fifth checkout request arrives, finds no free slot in the Payments Pool, and is rejected immediately with `503` instead of piling up memory and threads."
    send client > api "checkout #5"
    send api > client "503 Payments busy"
    callout api "Bounded blast radius"
  step cat-healthy "Catalog traffic stays completely healthy"
    "Because Catalog has its own isolated pool, browse requests still execute with normal latency. Without bulkheads, slow Payments calls would have drained a shared pool and taken down the entire site."
    send client > api "browse catalog"
    send api > p-cat "list items"
    send p-cat > cat "list"
    state p-cat,cat success
    focus p-cat,cat dim
    callout cat "Unaffected by Payments outage"
